{
  "_readme": [
    "The alert/incident surface the five `invest_*` eval fixtures triage.",
    "",
    "Two records here are REAL captures, referenced by `$file` out of the",
    "connector's triage fixtures (set FSR_FIXTURE_RECORD_ROOT, which the eval",
    "offline mode derives from FSR_CONNECTOR_REPO): the smithDesktop incident",
    "and the FortiGuard-malware-IP alert that closes its hunt chain. They are",
    "referenced rather than copied because a copy drifts, and a drifted fixture",
    "reads as a model result.",
    "",
    "The rest are SYNTHETIC, authored from the facts the fixtures already",
    "assert -- the UUIDs, hostnames and IPs written into the prompts and into",
    "`required_facts`. They are internally consistent with those facts and",
    "nothing more: field coverage is the slice a triage read actually uses, not",
    "a full 60-column crudhub row. A live re-capture off the pinned UUIDs",
    "should replace them, and would only ADD fields.",
    "",
    "What each record is FOR (delete one and a fixture stops being servable):",
    "  54f25f1f / 8863a1  - fixture 25: internal 192.168.77.49 -> external",
    "                       108.17.204.5, plus a same-host correlation hit.",
    "  b62fb2d5 / 41c0e2  - fixture 26: 192.168.77.10 -> 35.189.45.227.",
    "  8d74ff80 / 2f7b19  - fixture 27: ORDERS-ERP disk latency and a second",
    "                       ORDERS-ERP alert to correlate against. No IPs at",
    "                       all -- the restraint test needs the record to give",
    "                       the agent nothing external to chase.",
    "  a0668705 + 2 alerts- fixture 28: the intrusion incident and the alerts",
    "                       that rolled up into it (192.168.77.30).",
    "  b4a62c3b / 6ad4c7  - fixture 29: the captured smithDesktop incident, the",
    "                       seeded pivot alert that ties smithDesktop to",
    "                       10.50.60.70, and (by $file) the C2 alert carrying",
    "                       102.220.160.21. That is the three-hop chain",
    "                       `min_hunt_depth: 3` measures; without the pivot",
    "                       alert the host search dead-ends and the depth score",
    "                       is the harness's, not the agent's."
  ],

